  "prefLabel": "Bea 303.09 Website Design, Development, or Digital Experience Enhancements",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Bea 303.09 Website Design, Development, or Digital Experience Enhancements. In addition to the project requirements in Bea 303.02 above, applications that include design, development, or digital experience enhancements of a website shall:\n\n(a) Be clearly focused on tourism promotion and designed to attract visitors to New Hampshire;\n\n(b) Prominently display the words “New Hampshire”, the BEA generated logo, and link to visitnh.gov in its advertising campaigns on the website’s homepage;\n\n(c) Be produced by a professional vendor;\n\n(d) Include a copy of the contract for professional services;\n\n(e) Include a wireframe, design concepts, and navigation structure for the website; and\n\n(f) Be reviewed by the director of the DTTD, or the director’s designee, to ensure compliance with this section prior to the website going online.\n\nSource. #13270, eff 9-30-21; ss by #14624, eff 7-7-26, EXPIRES: 7-7-36 (formerly Bea 303.06)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/bea300.html"
